Work-order lifecycle
1. Open — a fault has been received.
2. Assigned — a manager assigns a technician.
3. In Progress — the technician starts work.
4. Awaiting Parts — work cannot continue yet.
5. Completed — technician records the repair.
6. Verified — an authorised person checks the work.
7. Closed — the work order is finalised.

A completed work order should require:
- Work performed.
- Resolution description.
- Completion date.
- Technician responsible.
- Optional photograph or evidence.
A fault should not be closed just because someone clicked a button. The system should preserve its complete history.

