25. What the finished application should look like as a whole













The overall experience should be consistent:
- The staff portal is structured, information-rich and efficient.
- The customer portal is welcoming and simple.
- The dashboard gives management an accurate picture of the scheme.
- Financial workflows are traceable.
- Meter readings and billing are logically connected.
- Faults move through a clear repair process.
- Infrastructure has a proper maintenance history.
- Pip gives the system a recognisable identity.
- The animations bring personality without sacrificing usability.
My strongest recommendation: do not start implementing all 15 modules at once. Build the application shell, design system and login first. Then build one complete workflow from beginning to end:

Register Customer → Create Connection → Record Meter → Submit Reading → Generate Invoice → Record Payment → Generate Receipt

Once that entire workflow works, you will have the foundation for the rest of the application.